<header><p class="st-kicker">theocracy · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Zaydi Imamate of Yemen</h1><p class="st-meta">897 CE – 1597 CE (approx.) · capital Sa'dah</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Zaydi Shi'a imamate founded at Sa'dah in 897, a religious state in the northern Yemeni highlands that lasted, in various forms, until 1962.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 897 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-hadi-ila-l-haqq-yahya">Yahya ibn al-Husayn</a>, a descendant of al-Hasan from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hejaz">Hejaz</a>, came to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saada">Sa'dah</a> at the invitation of feuding tribes. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">Imam</a> al-Hadi ila al-Haqq he settled their disputes and founded a Zaydi state, establishing the doctrine that any learned descendant of Ali and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatima">Fatima</a> who claimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">imamate</a> by rising against injustice could be imam.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">imamate</a> had no hereditary succession; rival claimants often contested it, and its reach rarely extended far beyond the northern highlands and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saada">Sa'dah</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">Imams</a> depended on the support of tribes such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hashid">Hashid</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakil">Bakil</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mansur-abdallah-ibn-hamza">al-Mansur Abd Allah ibn Hamza</a> in the 13th century revived its strength against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubids</a>, and it competed with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sulayhid-dynasty">Sulayhids</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rasulid-dynasty">Rasulids</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tahirid-dynasty">Tahirids</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">Imam</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mutawakkil-yahya-sharaf-al-din">Sharaf al-Din Yahya</a> expanded the state in the early 16th century, but the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> conquered most of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-yemen">Yemen</a> after 1538. In 1597 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasim-ibn-muhammad">al-Qasim ibn Muhammad</a> proclaimed himself imam and began the revolt that created the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qasimid-state">Qasimid State</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="theocracy, 897 CE – 1597 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M30 82 V46 Q50 12 70 46 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 30 V82 M40 58 H60"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">theocracy</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Arabia and the Gulf</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:77.55%;width:13.93%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>897 CE – 1597 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>theocracy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sa'dah</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>al-Hadi ila al-Haqq Yahya, al-Mansur Abd Allah ibn Hamza, Sharaf al-Din Yahya</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Zaydi Shi'a Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/yemen">Yemen</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rassid Imamate, Zaydi Imamate, Imamate of Yemen</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1247&amp;focus=zaydi-imamate-of-yemen" aria-label="Zaydi Imamate of Yemen on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5938 1615 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Zaydi Imamate of Yemen lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6207 1863h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6258 1871h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6258 1871h0"/></svg></a>